checkpoints/
# runs/ and results/ are both tracked on purpose, and the reason is verification.
# The networks here are small MLPs, so a checkpoint is 170 KB and all twelve come to
# 2.3 MB; the per-update train_log.jsonl files add another 296 KB. Shipping them means
# anyone can re-derive the reported numbers from the saved weights instead of retraining,
# and can read the learning curve update by update. See "Verifying the results" in
# RESULTS.md for the exact command. If the models ever grow past a few MB, revisit this.
data/
logs/
wandb/
outputs/
*.mp4
*.gif

.env
.env.*
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store

# scratch copies of configs made while sweeping hyperparameters
*.yaml.v1bak
